    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0822" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-04T13:00:00+08:00">May 4, 1933—1 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 4—4:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>401. Legation’s 380, April 27, 4 p.m.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d781-f1"/> Following
                    from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 3, 6 p.m. Japanese military now report that negotiations for
                            Nielsen’s release are not progressing satisfactorily and that the
                            commander at Siuyen has decided to resort to military measures at first
                            opportunity.</p>
                        <p>Owing to the difficulties of communication it seems advisable that
                            Consular officer visit Siuyen which is accessible only by aeroplane. In
                            response to my request the military state that availability of space on
                            military transport planes is extremely uncertain. However, they have
                            offered to assist this office to hire a special plane for the trip which
                            will cost a maximum of about yen 450. Propose sending Hall.<anchor
                                n="29" xml:id="d781-f2"/> Request authorization of
                                expenditure.”<anchor n="30" xml:id="d781-f3"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d781-f1" n="28" xml:id="d781-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d781-f2" n="29" xml:id="d781-f2-content">
                <p>Monroe B. Hall, Vice Consul at Mukden.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d781-f3" n="30" xml:id="d781-f3-content">
                <p>Authorization was given to the Minister In China in telegram No. 146, May 4, 6
                    p.m. (393.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/12).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
